{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence.bindingKernel_measure_eq_schwinger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence.bindingKernel_measure_eq_schwinger","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelConfluence.lean#L139-L162","doc":"**Bridge to the merged reduction class.** A binding kernel `Kb`\nsatisfying the (open) hypotheses of\n`BorelProperTimeMoment.BindingKernelSchwingerRepresentation` — positivity\nand the keystone-forced factorial `ds/s`-moments — determines, once\npackaged as a probability measure with the corresponding Stieltjes\nmoment data, the unit Schwinger measure: the two open conjecture\nhypotheses plus the classical Carleman theorem pin the kernel measure\nuniquely. This closes the loop `moments → measure` that the merged\n`kernel_moments_eq_schwinger` (moment-level indistinguishability) left\nat the moment level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence.balanced_kernel_tendsto_schwinger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence.balanced_kernel_tendsto_schwinger","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelConfluence.lean#L117-L137","doc":"**The balanced-kernel weak-convergence theorem (MAIN, conditional).**\nLet `K n` be the balanced q-Borel kernels along any sequence\n`q_n → 1⁺` — probability measures on `[0,∞)` with all moments finite —\nand suppose the `k`-th moments converge to `k!` (the audit-§2 balanced\nmoment confluence, exact at every order in the merged probe, here an\nexplicit hypothesis pending its own Lean tranche). Then, conditional on\nthe two classical Mathlib-gap theorems (Fréchet–Shohat + Carleman\ndeterminacy), the kernels converge WEAKLY to the unit Schwinger measure\n`e^{−s}·ds`. Positivity of the limit — the archimedean (POS) — is free:\nthe limit object is a `ProbabilityMeasure`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence.eq_schwingerMeasure_of_factorial_moments","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence.eq_schwingerMeasure_of_factorial_moments","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelConfluence.lean#L106-L115","doc":"**The determinacy pin (Attack A forcing, type-carried).** Any\nprobability measure on `ℝ` supported on `[0,∞)` whose moments are the\nkeystone-forced factorials IS the unit Schwinger measure — conditional\nonly on the classical Carleman theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence.stieltjesDeterminate_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence.stieltjesDeterminate_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelConfluence.lean#L95-L104","doc":"**Factorial-moment determinacy, conditional on classical Carleman.**\nThe Stieltjes moment problem for `{k!}` is determinate. The ONLY\nunformalized input is the classical Carleman–Stieltjes theorem (the\n`[CarlemanDeterminacyStieltjes]` hypothesis class, a Mathlib gap); its\ndivergence hypothesis is Lean-proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence.carlemanCondition_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence.carlemanCondition_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelConfluence.lean#L87-L93","doc":"**Carleman's condition holds for `{k!}`** — the general predicate of\nthe moment-problem infrastructure, discharged by the merged Attack-A\ndivergence proof (`BorelProperTimeMoment.carleman_divergence`). Nothing\nis re-derived: the instantiation is definitional. ","signatureChunk":0}]}